 the corrupted/GC state described in the issue, where keeping the original URL is the reasonable behavior. No public signature or default-behavior change: `.get(\"name\", self.url)` reproduces the original value whenever `\"name\"` is present. I found no evidence-backed defect in the patch; the only arguably relevant observation is that this patch does not add a regression test for the interleaved/GC scenario, which is not itself a code defect."},"token_usage":{"cached_tokens":360832,"estimated_cost_usd":0.0,"input_tokens":422093,"output_tokens":10897},"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{"end_line":430,"path":"locust/clients.py","start_line":300},"error":null,"name":"read_file","output_bytes":6296,"sequence":0,"succeeded":true},{"arguments":{"max_results":20,"query":"ResponseContextManager"},"error":null,"name":"find_symbols","output_bytes":4660,"sequence":1,"succeeded":true},{"arguments":{"max_results":30,"target":"locust/clients.py"},"error":null,"name":"find_related_tests","output_bytes":859,"sequence":2,"succeeded":true},{"arguments":{"end_line":300,"path":"locust/clients.py","start_line":1},"error":null,"name":"read_file","output_bytes":15654,"sequence":3,"succeeded":true},{"arguments":{"max_results":50,"symbol":"locust.clients.ResponseContextManager"},"error":null,"name":"find_references","output_bytes":2411,"sequence":4,"succeeded":true},{"arguments":{"max_results":100,"symbol":"request_meta"},"error":null,"name":"find_references","output_bytes":9112,"sequence":5,"succeeded":true},{"arguments":{"max_results":100,"pattern":"*.py","query":"request_meta"},"error":null,"name":"search_text","output_bytes":6344,"sequence":6,"succeeded":true},{"arguments":{"max_results":50,"pattern":"locust/clients.py","query":"\"name\""},"error":null,"name":"search_text","output_bytes":533,"sequence":7,"succeeded":true},{"arguments":{"end_line":340,"path":"locust/test/test_http.py","start_line":1},"error":null,"name":"read_file","output_bytes":15040,"sequence":8,"succeeded":true},{"argumen